{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01E1WNpRL1KTSBJEErus1aJP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DoupsZtoLZCQbfXsRwFcKu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add -A && git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfeat: US-059 - Fix: Keyboard shortcuts always show macOS modifiers (⌘/⌥/⌃) on Windows + Linux\n\nShortcutsModal, the toolbar tutor button, and the chat composer hint\nhard-coded the macOS glyphs (⌘/⌥/⌃/⇧) regardless of platform. The\nkeybind handler side was already correct (`isMod` accepts both metaKey\nand ctrlKey), so this is purely a display-layer fix.\n\n- New `src/lib/platform/platform.ts` helpers: `isMacPlatform(ua?)`,\n  `keyLabel(token, isMac)`, `modLabel(isMac)`, plus a `KeyToken` union\n  for semantic shortcut descriptors.\n- New `src/lib/platform/useIsMacPlatform()` SSR-safe hook (defaults\n  `false`, flips after `useEffect` reads `navigator.userAgent`).\n- ShortcutsModal now stores semantic tokens (`'mod'`, `'shift'`,\n  `'enter'`, etc.) and translates per-platform at render time. Modal\n  root gains `data-platform` for browser-test assertions.\n- TutorToolbarButton extracted; renders `⌘.` on mac vs `Ctrl+.` on\n  Windows/Linux. LessonChat hint and test-code-runner page updated to\n  use `modLabel(isMac)`.\n- Tests: 18 new in `platform.test.ts` (including the bug-repro group\n  asserting non-mac labels are `Ctrl/Alt/Shift`, NOT `⌘/⌥/⇧`); 4 new\n  in `useKeyboardShortcuts.test.ts` locking in `isMod`'s acceptance of\n  ctrlKey alongside metaKey.\n\nVerified end-to-end with playwright across two userAgent contexts\n(Windows + macOS) — see scripts/ralph/progress.txt for the assertion\nmatrix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"","description":"Commit US-059 changes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":207,"cache_read_input_tokens":137783,"cache_c